    "notes": "Tuning, inharmonicity, loss-model effective string length, and decay use mf and ff recordings at C2, C3, Gb3, C4, C5, Eb5, C6, A6, and C7. Values between anchors use linear interpolation. Low-bass loss values blend back to the generic model at A0; upper values use the C7 anchor. Felt frequencies use non-harmonic attack-residual centers shared by the same notes, not isolated felt measurements. The short bridge, body, FDN, damper, radiation, and sympathetic values stay modeled because the source has no isolated body impulse, pedal sweep, or dry room reference."
